WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.740
This video explains how to&nbsp;
make comments on the proposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.520
submission Teignbridge local plan 2020-2040

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:15.540
the live consultation Teignbridge local&nbsp;
plan web page contains links to all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.500
the consultation documents including&nbsp;
the proposed submission local plan

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.580
if you wish to make comments on any of the&nbsp;
consultation documents so scroll down this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:33.060
page until you see the start button, to begin&nbsp;
adding your comments click the start button

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.340
to comment you can log in with&nbsp;
your Teignbridge MyAccount

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.880
you can either create a MyAccount or continue&nbsp;
without one, please note that if you do not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:52.680
have a MyAccount you will not be able to&nbsp;
save and return to your comments later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.600
before you are able to proceed you&nbsp;
need to read the Privacy notice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.060
by pressing continue you are agreeing&nbsp;
to the conditions set out in this notice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:10.380
please select whether you are an agent acting on&nbsp;
behalf of someone else or making your own comments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:17.700
if you are an agent making comments on behalf of&nbsp;
someone else please fill in both sets of contact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:25.620
details if you are filling in your own form please&nbsp;
include all your contact details as requested we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:30.240
cannot accept anonymous representations&nbsp;
at this stage of the local plan process

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.540
you will need to select whether you wish&nbsp;
to comment on the local plan or Community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:44.940
infrastructure Levy from the drop down menu please&nbsp;
select which part of the local plan or which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:51.060
consultation document you wish to comment on you&nbsp;
can comment on specific aspects of the local plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.460
the whole local plan other consultation&nbsp;
documents or supporting evidence

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.780
you must then select which policy or proposal you&nbsp;
would like to comment on in the drop down menu

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:13.260
you are asked to comment whether you consider the&nbsp;
plan or policy to be legally compliant there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:19.020
many tests of legal compliance such as whether a&nbsp;
plan accords with national legislation has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:24.300
properly consulted on during its preparation&nbsp;
and has taken account of comments received

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.980
you are asked to comment whether you&nbsp;
consider the plan or policy to be sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.500
the national planning policy framework&nbsp;
sets out the tests of soundness to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:43.020
one whether the plan has been positively&nbsp;
prepared and meets the area's development needs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:49.920
two whether the plan is Justified being based on&nbsp;
evidence and considering reasonable alternatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:55.320
three whether the plan is effective&nbsp;
and enables sustainable development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.020
and four whether the plan is consistent&nbsp;
with national planning policy

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:07.680
you are asked to consider whether the&nbsp;
plan complies with the duty to cooperate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.980
this duty ensures that neighbouring authorities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:16.140
and certain statutory organisations are&nbsp;
involved during the preparation of the plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:23.640
consider that the plan does not meet these three&nbsp;
requirements you must explain your reasons why

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:31.140
if you have completed question three you&nbsp;
can also set out any modifications that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:36.120
you consider would need to be needed to&nbsp;
make the plan legally compliant or sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.180
once you have written your comments you&nbsp;
will need to press the add comments button&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.640
when you have added all your comments you&nbsp;
will need to press the next button to continue

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.180
Community infrastructure Levy&nbsp;
or CIL draft charging schedule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:02.460
review the proposed changes and indicates whether&nbsp;
you agree or not you will be asked if you wish to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:07.260
appear at the examination hearing that will&nbsp;
be held by an independent planning inspector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:12.960
if you choose not to appear at the hearing your&nbsp;
comments will still be considered by the inspector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.960
before you submit your comments you will be&nbsp;
asked to complete some information about yourself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.000
you can choose whether to provide&nbsp;
this information or not you must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.300
then click the submit button to send us your&nbsp;
comments thank you for watching this video

